  "notes": "LightGBM and CatBoost with Huber loss (alpha=1e-3, ~0.5σ of y) replace L2/RMSE in the same 5-seed + DE-asym pipeline as T75/T89 to deliver +4.56 / +1.76 LOSO standalone respectively, and +4.63 LOSO in the iter_016 4-way ensemble. The improvement comes from reducing the regressor's pull toward large-|y| tail samples (under class-balanced weights), letting it predict more accurately near the EV-gate threshold. CRUCIAL FINDING: T89 (CB RMSE) HARMS the ensemble when CB_Huber is present — it should be dropped entirely. The largest diversification benefits come from T87 (NN SPO+, 0.79 corr) and T95 (GRU, 0.40 corr). LGB_Huber and CB_Huber have 0.95 corr but their joint contribution is still positive (+0.27 LOSO). Custom SPO+ subgradient code is implemented but unrun; built-in Huber wins are sufficient for iter_016."
